n {:value "313006"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "353606"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19009100"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/311"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Individual All-Around, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "27 – 31 July 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2166"} "Bercy Arena, Bercy, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2012200"} "44 from 23 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "A few months after claiming gold in Tokyo, " [:a {:href "/athletes/144639"} "Daiki Hashimoto"] " had been defeated at the 2021 World Championships in Kitakyushu by China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/152584"} "Zhang Boheng"] ". Hashimoto struck back in 2022, pushing Zhang back to second place, and won again in 2023, with Zhang absent. In Paris, Zhang was back, leading the qualifying, with Hashimoto in third, behind his teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/152665"} "Shinnosuke Oka"] ". " [:a {:href "/athletes/141858"} "Xiao Ruoteng"] ", the Tokyo silver medalist, had qualified in fourth."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Zhang started poorly on floor (13.233) due to a botched landing. Hashimoto then fell from the pommel horse, and then had a mediocre performance on the rings that moved him out of contention. However, former junior World Champion Oka performed steadily and, with only the horizontal bar to go, led the field, but with Zhang and Xiao following closely. Zhang was the last to perform, needing to gain 0.467 to pass Oka. Zhang went for the toughest exercise of the field (a 6.5 D-score) and ranked first in the field on the bar. However, his 14.633 was only 0.133 better than Oka, giving the Japanese a surprise gold."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Oka’s gold was the fourth consecutive gold medal in the men’s individual all-around for Japan, after Hashimoto (2021) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/111925"} "Kohei Uchimura"] " in 2012 and 2016."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/152665"} "Shinnosuke Oka"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/152584"} "Zhang Boheng"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/141858"} "Xiao Ruoteng"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147073"} "Illia Kovtun"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/UKR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/UKR.png"}] "UKR"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143148"} "Joe Fraser"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "6"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/144639"} "Daiki 